BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ammouliani-ammouliani-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-ammouliani-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Nikolaos (patron)\, Ammouliani
LOCATION:Ammouliani\, Ammouliani\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The historic church of Agios Nikolaos\, restored in 2022 with funds from shipowner Athanasios Martinos\, is the island's parish church and its patron's feast on 5-6 December is the one winter day the fishing village fills up\, with vespers\, liturgy and a blessing at the harbour. The ferry from Tripiti takes ten minutes and runs all year.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ammouliani/#ammouliani-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-ammouliani
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ammouliani/#ammouliani-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-ammouliani
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:anafi-chora-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Nikolaos\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Anafi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Anafi's patron saint has his church on the main square of Chora and the island keeps his day\, 6 December\, with a liturgy and a formal communal meal organised by the cultural association. It's a residents' winter feast — a handful of visitors at most — and reaching the island in December depends on the weekly Santorini boat and the weather.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/anafi/#chora-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/anafi/#chora-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-koumbara-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-koumbara-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Nikolaos\, Koumbara
LOCATION:Koumbara\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of the sailors' saint at Koumbara beach\, west of the port\, is where Ios celebrates 6 December: liturgy\, then food and wine for the handful of islanders who are around in winter. Worth knowing if you are on Ios out of season.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#koumbara-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-koumbara
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#koumbara-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-koumbara
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Nikolaos\, patron of Agios Nikolaos town
LOCATION:Agios Nikolaos\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The town named after the saint keeps 6 December as its patronal feast: vespers on the 5th\, hierarchical liturgy and a procession of the icon through the centre and along the lake on the 6th\, with the municipal band and school parades\, and the town's Christmas lights switched on around the same days. The tiny 8th-century chapel of Agios Nikolaos at the Minos Beach headland\, which gave the town its name\, also holds a liturgy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schoinoussa-mersini-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-mersini-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Nikolaos\, Mersini
LOCATION:Mersini\, Schoinoussa\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port of Mersini celebrates the sailors' saint on 6 December with a liturgy and a communal meal for the islanders who winter on Schinoussa. Worth knowing only if you are there in December.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/schoinoussa/#mersini-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-mersini
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/schoinoussa/#mersini-panigiri-of-agios-nikolaos-mersini
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-skiathos-town-lighting-of-the-christmas-boat-bourtzi-skiatho-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Lighting of the Christmas boat\, Bourtzi\, Skiathos Town
LOCATION:Skiathos Town\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Skiathos\, a sailors' island\, decorates boats rather than trees: on St Nicholas' day\, 6 December\, the municipality lights the big illuminated boat by the Bourtzi at the old port at 8 pm and switches on the town lights\, with carols and a stall or two\, and smaller lit boats appear in house windows. It opens a month of Christmas events at the Bourtzi cultural centre (bazaars\, Karagiozis\, school plays). Ferries run a reduced winter schedule from Volos and Agios Konstantinos\, so check them first.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-lighting-of-the-christmas-boat-bourtzi-skiatho
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-lighting-of-the-christmas-boat-bourtzi-skiatho
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:elafonisos-elafonisos-harbour-church-feast-of-agios-spyridon-patron-of--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271213
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Spyridon\, patron of Elafonisos
LOCATION:Elafonisos (harbour church)\, Elafonisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The patron's winter feast at the church of Agios Spyridon on the harbour on 12 December: vespers on the 11th\, liturgy and a procession of the icon along the quay on the 12th\, and a reception offered by the parish. The island has a few hundred winter residents and one or two kafeneia open\; the ferry from Pounta runs all year.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#elafonisos-harbour-church-feast-of-agios-spyridon-patron-of-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#elafonisos-harbour-church-feast-of-agios-spyridon-patron-of-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kasos-fry-panigiri-of-agios-spyridon-fry-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271213
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Spyridon\, Fry
LOCATION:Fry\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port town's own winter panigiri\, on 11-12 December at the church of Agios Spyridon in Fry\, with vespers and a glendi indoors with lyra\, sweets and wine. One of the few times to see Kasos with only Kasiots on it.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#fry-panigiri-of-agios-spyridon-fry
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#fry-panigiri-of-agios-spyridon-fry
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zakynthos-zakynthos-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-his-dormition-zakynt-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271216
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271219
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Dionysios (his dormition)\, Zakynthos town
LOCATION:Zakynthos town\, Zakynthos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The winter feast of the patron: after the liturgy on 17 December the incorrupt body is carried through the town to Solomos Square and back via Agios Markos with the philharmonics of Zakynthos\, Artemision and Alykes\, the schools and a dozen visiting bishops\; the body stays out for veneration for two more days before being returned to its silver casket. Cold\, crowded and very Zakynthian\; the pastry shops around Agios Markos do the best mandolato.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/zakynthos/#zakynthos-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-his-dormition-zakynt
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/zakynthos/#zakynthos-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-his-dormition-zakynt
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
